BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Conor Janda's Bloomington Debut!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260911T210000
UID:20260911-conor-janda-s-bloomington-debut-1900
DESCRIPTION:Conor Janda is a stand-up\, writer\, and actor. His writing ex
 emplifies both the neuroses of a New York transplant and the fiery spirit 
 of a Philadelphia native. Conor can be seen on Netflix in Kevin Hart's Fun
 ny AF\, on Don't Tell Comedy's channel\, and was recently named a New Face
  of Comedy at the Just for Laughs Festival in Montreal. He has been featur
 ed as a writer and actor on the Gag\, Comedy Central’s queer digital cha
 nnel. Conor’s stand up covers everything from having a stay at home dad 
 to going to an all boys Catholic school to getting sober from alcohol. He 
 is too anxious to be at a Fire Island Underwear Party or a Philadelphia Ea
 gles tailgate\, which may be the only thing bridging those communities\, a
  glimmer of unity in these divided times that Conor is happy to provide. W
 hen he’s not touring around the country\, Conor is the co-creator\, writ
 er\, and star of web series BOYS CLUB with friend and collaborator Nico Ca
 rney\, which can and should be watched on YouTube.  BOYS CLUB was origina
 lly developed as a series with Imagine Entertainment and Scott King. One t
 ime\, someone kind of famous said he was too kind to be as funny as he is.
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.comedyattic.com/shows/376170
X-SOURCE:The Comedy Attic
END:VEVENT
